{"findings":[{"pattern_id":"1.1","pattern_name":"Pointer-based std::sort / std::stable_sort","category":"sorting","tier":1,"severity":"MEDIUM","severity_default":"HIGH","file":"mscts/mstap/msTapSubtreeSyn.cc","line":285,"title":"Distance-only node sort ties pick arbitrary load for 1/4 repeater anchor","description_md":"`termDistVec` holds `msTapSubtreeSynthesis::node` wrappers around `ndmTerm*`. `std::sort` uses `node::operator<`, which compares only `_dist` (descending). When multiple loads share the same driver distance, tie order is unspecified. The odd-load branch walks the sorted vector to choose `load1`, then calls `instantiateRepeater(driver, load1, …)` at one-quarter distance toward the driver.","snippet_ctx":"  for(termVecType::iterator itr = loadTerms.begin(); itr != loadTerms.end(); ++itr) {
    ...
    termDistances.push_back(n);
  }
  std::sort(termDistances.begin(), termDistances.end());
  ...
  status = instantiateRepeater(driver, load1, 0, target, level);","realness":"real","downstream_observability_md":"Sorted `termDistances` drives selection of `load1` and the computed `target` coordinate for `instantiateRepeater`, mutating the MSCTS tap subtree topology and downstream latency/skew.","controls_md":"MSCTS multisource tap subtree synthesis (`msTapSubtreeSynthesis::run` → clustering/repeater insertion). Triggered when a driver fanout group has an odd load count and two or more loads share equal distance to the driver.","performance_note_md":"Add O(1) tie-break on `ndmTerm::getId()` (or `ndmObjPtrCmpType`) inside `node::operator<` or the call-site lambda; no extra sort pass or container copy.","fix_versions":[{"label":"Version A (Simple)","code_md":"```cpp
std::sort(termDistances.begin(), termDistances.end(),
  [](const node& a, const node& b) {
    if (a.getDist() != b.getDist()) return a.getDist() > b.getDist();
    return a.getObj()->getId() < b.getObj()->getId();
  });
```"},{"label":"Version B (Robust)","code_md":"```cpp
// Extend msTapSynthesis.h node::operator< with ndmObjPtrCmpType{} tie-break
bool operator<(const node& n) const {
  if (_dist != n._dist) return _dist > n._dist;
  return ndmObjPtrCmpType{}(_obj, n._obj);
}
```"}],"rationale_md":"Equal-distance symmetric loads are common in gridded layouts; tie order currently decides which sink anchors the first repeater and where it is placed.","false_positive_check_md":"Element type is `node`, not raw `T*`; still a Pattern 1.1 pack hit because sort uses a non-identity key without deterministic tie-break. Not neutralized; not debug-only."},{"pattern_id":"1.1","pattern_name":"Pointer-based std::sort / std::stable_sort","category":"sorting","tier":1,"severity":"MEDIUM","severity_default":"HIGH","file":"mscts/mstap/msTapSubtreeSyn.cc","line":805,"title":"Distance-only node sort ties split loads across recursive clusters","description_md":"In `doClustering`, loads are wrapped in `node` objects keyed by X or Y coordinate distance and sorted with the same distance-only `operator<`. Equal-distance loads receive arbitrary relative order; the first `size1` entries go to `loadTerms1` and the remainder to `loadTerms2`, driving recursive `doClustering` splits.","snippet_ctx":"      node n(load, dis, loc);
      termDis.push_back(n);
    }
    std::sort(termDis.begin(), termDis.end());
    unsigned int size1 = baseCount*(q/2+q_r);
    ...
    doClustering(driver, loadTerms1, level, useSplit4, dir);
    doClustering(driver, loadTerms2, level, useSplit4, dir);","realness":"real","downstream_observability_md":"Partition boundary between `loadTerms1` and `loadTerms2` depends on sort order among tied distances, changing recursive tap-tree topology and wirelength/latency QoR.","controls_md":"MSCTS tap subtree synthesis when fanout exceeds `baseCount` (2 or 4). Most visible when many loads share the same coordinate on the active split axis.","performance_note_md":"Same single-comparator tie-break as line 285; no additional allocations.","fix_versions":[{"label":"Version A (Simple)","code_md":"```cpp
std::sort(termDis.begin(), termDis.end(),
  [](const node& a, const node& b) {
    if (a.getDist() != b.getDist()) return a.getDist() > b.getDist();
    return a.getObj()->getId() < b.getObj()->getId();
  });
```"}],"rationale_md":"Cluster membership is order-sensitive; unspecified tie order directly changes which sinks are co-clustered.","false_positive_check_md":"Not a value-type sort; not using `ndmObjPtrCmpType` today. Downstream recursive clustering is order-sensitive."},{"pattern_id":"1.9","pattern_name":"std::min_element / max_element on pointer vector with pointer tiebreak","category":"container","tier":1,"severity":"MEDIUM","severity_default":"MEDIUM","file":"ctscto/ctosc/ctoscLoadPartition.cc","line":136,"title":"SP sink min_element lacks term-ID tie-break on equal delays","description_md":"After sorting `_sinks` by late margin, `std::min_element` selects the shortest-path (minimum early) sink using a lambda that compares early then late delays but returns `false` for full ties. Among equal-delay sinks, the first in `_sinks` wins; `_sinks` order comes from `allSinks` fanout collection without canonical term ordering at ties.","snippet_ctx":"  auto spSinkIt = std::min_element(_sinks.begin(), _sinks.end(),
    [&](ndmTerm* sink1, ndmTerm* sink2){ ... return l1<l2; });
  _spSinkPos = std::distance(_sinks.begin(), spSinkIt);
  ...
  if (... _spSinkPos < boundary)) { appendBinaryPartitions(...); }","realness":"real","downstream_observability_md":"`_spSinkPos` gates whether binary partition solutions include the critical SP load (`appendBinaryPartitions`, `haveToInclude` paths). Different tied-sink choice changes buffered-load partitions and MTCTO GLS buffering QoR.","controls_md":"MTCTO load partitioning init when `_enableBinaryPartition` or single-load fallback paths run; requires two or more sinks with identical early/late delays at the representative sclk/corner.","performance_note_md":"Add final `return ndmObjPtrCmpType{}(sink1, sink2);` in the lambda; O(1) per comparison.","fix_versions":[{"label":"Version A (Simple)","code_md":"```cpp
auto spSinkIt = std::min_element(_sinks.begin(), _sinks.end(),
  [&](ndmTerm* s1, ndmTerm* s2) {
    ... existing early/late checks ...
    if (l1 != l2) return l1 < l2;
    return ndmObjPtrCmpType{}(s1, s2);
  });
```"}],"rationale_md":"Partition feasibility explicitly special-cases the SP sink index; tie-breaking must be stable.","false_positive_check_md":"Custom comparator present but incomplete at full ties. Element type is `ndmTerm*`; downstream mutation path confirmed at lines 946 and 1422."},{"pattern_id":"1.9","pattern_name":"std::min_element / max_element on pointer vector with pointer tiebreak","category":"container","tier":1,"severity":"MEDIUM","severity_default":"MEDIUM","file":"ctscto/ctosc/ctomt/ctomtReloc.cc","line":868,"title":"Max path-delay element picks first tied load for relocation vector","description_md":"`std::max_element` on `pathDelayVec` (float) uses default `operator<`. Tied maximum delays select the first index, mapped to `groupedLoads[maxIdx]` built from `ctsOutArcIterator` fanout order. That term sets the "max delay direction" candidate location in Gskew relocation.","snippet_ctx":"  size_t maxIdx = std::distance(pathDelayVec.begin(),
    std::max_element(pathDelayVec.begin(), pathDelayVec.end()));
  ndmTerm *maxTerm = groupedLoads[maxIdx];
  ...
  candidates.push_back(criticalMaxDirLoc);","realness":"real","downstream_observability_md":"`addCriticalPathCandidates` → `generateCandidateLocations` → `filterAndAddCandidates` → `newDrvTermLocVec` feeds driver relocation in `getTargetLocsForGskew`, affecting sizing/placement QoR.","controls_md":"MTCTO Gskew relocation strategy (`ctomtReloc::getTargetLocsForGskew`) when multiple grouped loads share the same maximum average path delay.","performance_note_md":"Use indexed max with `(delay, -termId)` lexicographic compare or tie-break inside a single linear scan; no sorting required.","fix_versions":[{"label":"Version A (Simple)","code_md":"```cpp
size_t maxIdx = 0;
for (size_t i = 1; i < pathDelayVec.size(); ++i) {
  if (pathDelayVec[i] > pathDelayVec[maxIdx] ||
      (pathDelayVec[i] == pathDelayVec[maxIdx] &&
       groupedLoads[i]->getId() < groupedLoads[maxIdx]->getId())) {
    maxIdx = i;
  }
}
```"}],"rationale_md":"Critical-path direction candidates bias relocation; tied maxima should not depend on arc iteration order.","false_positive_check_md":"Parallel float vector + pointer vector; not a value-only sink. Min-element sibling at line 882 shares the same tie class."},{"pattern_id":"1.9","pattern_name":"std::min_element / max_element on pointer vector with pointer tiebreak","category":"container","tier":1,"severity":"MEDIUM","severity_default":"MEDIUM","file":"ctscto/ctosc/ctomt/ctomtReloc.cc","line":882,"title":"Min path-delay element picks first tied load for relocation vector","description_md":"Symmetric to the max-delay site: `std::min_element` on `pathDelayVec` selects the first minimum, mapped to `groupedLoads[minIdx]` for the "min delay direction" relocation candidate.","snippet_ctx":"  size_t minIdx = std::distance(pathDelayVec.begin(),
    std::min_element(pathDelayVec.begin(), pathDelayVec.end()));
  ndmTerm *minTerm = groupedLoads[minIdx];
  ...
  candidates.push_back(criticalMinDirLoc);","realness":"real","downstream_observability_md":"Same relocation pipeline as line 868; min-direction candidate coordinates feed `newDrvTermLocVec` and driver move evaluation.","controls_md":"MTCTO Gskew relocation when two or more loads share identical minimum average path delay.","performance_note_md":"Paired linear scan with deterministic term-id tie-break; can merge with max scan in one loop.","fix_versions":[{"label":"Version A (Simple)","code_md":"```cpp
size_t minIdx = 0;
for (size_t i = 1; i < pathDelayVec.size(); ++i) {
  if (pathDelayVec[i] < pathDelayVec[minIdx] ||
      (pathDelayVec[i] == pathDelayVec[minIdx] &&
       groupedLoads[i]->getId() < groupedLoads[minIdx]->getId())) {
    minIdx = i;
  }
}
```"}],"rationale_md":"Min and max critical-path anchors should both be canonical under delay ties.","false_positive_check_md":"Default float comparison only; pointer identity reached via `groupedLoads` index."},{"pattern_id":"1.9","pattern_name":"std::min_element / max_element on pointer vector with pointer tiebreak","category":"container","tier":1,"severity":"MEDIUM","severity_default":"MEDIUM","file":"ctscto/ctoUtil.cc","line":4384,"title":"Min path-delay index gates SP filter candidate gain acceptance","description_md":"`calculateNewDrvTermLocationForSpFilter` uses two-argument `std::min_element` on `loadPathDelayVec`. Tied minima pick the first load index, which defines `minDelayIndx` used to gate whether candidate driver locations achieve positive gain (`bboxVec[minDelayIndx]` check).","snippet_ctx":"  std::vector<float>::iterator it =
    std::min_element(std::begin(loadPathDelayVec), std::end(loadPathDelayVec));
  int minDelayIndx = std::distance(std::begin(loadPathDelayVec), it);
  ...
  if (bboxVec[minDelayIndx].getDistanceToPoint(loc) <= origDistVec[minDelayIndx]) {
    gainVec[i]=0; continue;
  }","realness":"real","downstream_observability_md":"`minDelayIndx` filters which relocation candidates survive gain scoring; survivors populate `newDrvTermLocVec` consumed by MTCTO skew relocation (`ctomtReloc` SP-filter path).","controls_md":"CTO SP-filter relocation when `calculateNewDrvTermLocationForSpFilter` runs and multiple loads share the minimum path delay.","performance_note_md":"Replace with single-pass min index plus term-id tie-break using parallel load vector; avoids sort.","fix_versions":[{"label":"Version A (Simple)","code_md":"```cpp
int minDelayIndx = 0;
for (int i = 1; i < cntLoad; ++i) {
  if (loadPathDelayVec[i] < loadPathDelayVec[minDelayIndx] ||
      (loadPathDelayVec[i] == loadPathDelayVec[minDelayIndx] &&
       loadLocVec[i].getX() < loadLocVec[minDelayIndx].getX())) { // or term id
    minDelayIndx = i;
  }
}
```"}],"rationale_md":"Reference load for gain filtering must not depend on input vector order when delays tie.","false_positive_check_md":"Float vector, but index selects among parallel loads with distinct geometry; downstream QoR path confirmed."}],"dismissed_buckets":[{"pattern_id":"1.1","bucket_label":"Value-type / pair-key sorts (int, float, enum, pair first-member)","count":178,"rationale_md":"Production pack hits on `int` indices (`soSolverUpdater`), `float` slacks/medians (`soCG`, `soMacroDelay`, `msCto`, `msSplit*`, `ctoFlow`, `ctoLog`, `ctsSession`, `ctsLocalSkew`, `ctsNdrMgr` pairs), `grNodeId` tuples (`fmaxCgSolver`), percentile vectors (`fmaxLpSolver*`), and median coords (`msClustering`, `msAutoTapFlow` grids). All deterministic or non-pointer keys. Sample: `ccd/skewopt/soSolverUpdater.cc:272`, `ccd/ctsccd/fmax/fmaxLpSolver.cc:3581`, `ctsutil/ctsSession.cc:2802`."},{"pattern_id":"1.1","bucket_label":"Existing deterministic ID/name comparators","count":24,"rationale_md":"Pack sites already pass project comparators: `ndmObjPtrCmpType` (`soClockGateOpt`, `soLogicCone`, `ctoLocalSkewMgr`, `msMerge`), `modCompare`/`modCompareByName` (CTO/MTCTO sizing), `ConstraintComparatorNew`, `CompareTracks`, `CompareSinkDistToParent`, `flowClockBagCmp`, `ctsModuleCompare` tie-break in `modCompare`. Sample: `ccd/skewopt/soClockGateOpt.cc:401`, `ctscto/ctoFlow.cc:8313`."},{"pattern_id":"1.1","bucket_label":"Unit tests and debug-only sorts","count":18,"rationale_md":"Skipped per scope: `ccd/ctsccd/fmax/unittest/*`, verbose `lpTreePlacerImpl` cout diagnostics, commented sorts in `fmaxLpSolverIncremental.cc`. Sample: `ccd/ctsccd/fmax/unittest/fmaxCostFunctionsTest.cc:576`."},{"pattern_id":"1.1","bucket_label":"Deterministic value-type tie-break via pair second member","count":12,"rationale_md":"`std::pair<size_t,int>` / `pair<float,int>` / `pair<size_t,KeyType>` sorts in fmax endpoint/variable picking use lexicographic pair order; second member is stable variable index/key. Sample: `ccd/ctsccd/fmax/fmaxLpSolverCompressedEndpoints.cc:2305`, `ccd/ctsccd/fmax/fmaxEndpointCompression.cc:153`."},{"pattern_id":"1.9","bucket_label":"Value-type extrema or custom comparator with deterministic logic","count":11,"rationale_md":"`ccd/ctsccd/ccdSubtree.cc` max on integer scenario counts (index tie-break is deterministic); `ccd/skewopt/soClockGraph.cc:733` uses custom size comparator; `ctscto/ctoFlow.cc:121` int levels; `ctoscLoadPartition.cc:967` size_t min boundary; `ctscto/ctoUtil.cc:5190` median on floats only; `mscts/mstap/msFlexibleTapPartition.cc:945/1019` debug `printf` only."},{"pattern_id":"1.11","bucket_label":"std::unique preceded by deterministic sort or on value types","count":12,"rationale_md":"Sites pair canonical sort with unique: `soClockGateOpt` (`ndmObjPtrCmpType`), `soMacroDelay` (scenario value sort), `msMerge` (`ndmObjPtrCmpType`), `msPreroutes` (`CompareTracks`), `msTapCellMgr` (coord/id lambda sort on int nodes), `msuiCommands` (`LessName`/`SameName`), `fmaxLpSolverIncremental` (`ConstraintComparatorNew`), `ccduiReport` (int node ids), `msAutoTapFlow` (int grids). Sample: `ccd/skewopt/soClockGateOpt.cc:402`, `mscts/msmesh/msMerge.cc:251`."},{"pattern_id":"1.11","bucket_label":"Ineffective or non-mutating std::unique (result discarded)","count":2,"rationale_md":"`ctscto/ctoFlow.cc:2774` and `ctscto/ctoArea.cc:610` call `std::unique` without assigning/erasing; they do not canonicalize pointer vectors. Any order sensitivity comes from upstream traversal, not Pattern 1.11 unique semantics. Dead-code/no-op unique."},{"pattern_id":"1.11","bucket_label":"Value-type unique (int indices / dedup)","count":3,"rationale_md":"`soSolverUpdater` `selectedToInfos` (`vector<int>`), `soDesign` `masterClocks` (`cstrClock` value handles with `operator<`). Sample: `ccd/skewopt/soSolverUpdater.cc:273`, `ccd/skewopt/soDesign.cc:9123`."}]}

